{"term":{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000587","compactId":"SO_0000587","id":"SO:0000587","label":"group_I_intron","definition":{"text":"Group I catalytic introns are large self-splicing ribozymes. They catalyze their own excision from mRNA, tRNA and rRNA precursors in a wide range of organisms. The core secondary structure consists of 9 paired regions (P1-P9). These fold to essentially two domains, the P4-P6 domain (formed from the stacking of P5, P4, P6 and P6a helices) and the P3-P9 domain (formed from the P8, P3, P7 and P9 helices). Group I catalytic introns often have long ORFs inserted in loop regions.","xrefs":["http://www.sanger.ac.uk/cgi-bin/Rfam/getacc?RF00028"]},"comments":["GO:0000372."],"synonyms":[{"scope":"exact","value":"group I intron"}],"xrefs":["http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_I_intron"],"subsets":["SOFA"],"altIds":[],"namespace":"sequence","isObsolete":false,"replacedBy":[],"canonicalUrl":"/browser/current_release/term/SO:0000587/","history":{"firstSeen":{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files"},"mostRecent":{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files"},"entries":[{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files"}]},"parents":["SO:0000588"],"children":[],"ancestors":["SO:0000588","SO:0000188","SO:0000835","SO:0000833","SO:0001411","SO:0000001","SO:0000110"],"descendants":[],"relationships":[],"graphNeighborhood":{"parents":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000588"],"children":[],"related":[]}},"graph":{"parents":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000588","id":"SO:0000588","label":"SO:0000588"}],"children":[],"related":[]}}